Left over from k321 (secrets worker, 2026-10-31), secrets lane. k321 makes `ocp keys secure` run all of validate() first. Two paths stay unchecked on purpose and still die inside Perl ("Not a HASH reference ... internal error") before PIN2 on `control_planes: ['host']` or `workers: 'host'`:
- `ocp keys secure --drop-bootstrap` on a project that is secure already (deliberately not gated by k321: it is the step after a leaked bootstrap key);
- `ocp keys operator add|rm`, which uses the same machine lookup.
Nothing changes on disk or on a machine, but the user gets an internal error instead of validate()'s line.

Fix as k323 did for destroy: check only what those paths read (the machine lookup's shapes), with validate()'s words, before anything is asked or touched. Done = tests for both shapes on both paths: validate()'s line, exit 1, no prompt, no SSH.

